  "summary": "This paper compares seven free-standing Ti3C2Tx paper electrodes: pristine Ti3C2Tx, mixed and alternating-filtered sandwich-like SWCNT and MWCNT composites, plus sandwich-like OLC and rGO composites. Ti3C2Tx was produced by 50 wt% HF etching of Ti3AlC2, followed by DMSO intercalation and sonication delamination; composite papers were prepared by vacuum filtration. The highest reported volumetric capacitance was 435 F cm\u22123 for Sandwich-like Ti3C2Tx/rGO at 2 mV s\u22121 in 1 M MgSO4. Areal capacitance, mass loading, BET surface area, pore diameter, porosity, and true (002) d-spacing were not reported."
